(The OSI Model) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The OSI model is a seven layer framework that describes how data moves across a network.) Tj T*
(The physical layer sends raw bits over a cable or radio link. The network layer chooses) Tj T*
(a path for packets between different networks. The transport layer provides end to end) Tj T*
(delivery between applications on two hosts. Encapsulation means each layer wraps the) Tj T*
(data from the layer above with its own header.) Tj T*
