(TCP and UDP) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(TCP is a connection oriented protocol that guarantees reliable, ordered delivery of) Tj T*
(data. Before sending data, TCP performs a three way handshake using SYN, SYN-ACK and ACK) Tj T*
(segments. UDP is a connectionless protocol that sends datagrams without guaranteeing) Tj T*
(delivery or order. Video calls and online games often use UDP because low latency) Tj T*
(matters more than retransmitting lost packets.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
