(IP Addressing and Subnets) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An IP address is a numeric label that identifies a device on a network. IPv4 addresses) Tj T*
(are 32 bits long, while IPv6 addresses are 128 bits long. A subnet mask separates the) Tj T*
(network portion of an address from the host portion. NAT lets many devices on a private) Tj T*
(network share a single public IP address.) Tj T*
ET
